    "id": "prop:certificate-infeasibility",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Exactly one alternative holds for the oracle-instance \\(\\mathsf X_{\\mathrm{phys}}\\): either the feasible-case theorem returns \\(E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star}\\), or \\(\\operatorname{Opt}_{\\mathrm{sw}}=+\\infty\\).  The latter occurs if and only if \\(\\operatorname{Acc}_{\\mathrm{sw}}(Q,E_{\\mathrm{sw}};G)=0\\) for every switching certificate of length at most \\(B_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\), and equivalently if and only if no finite correctly typed generic acquired collection makes the full unconditional \\(\\operatorname{CTFIDU}^{+}\\) run accept.  Exhaustive enumeration decides the alternative in time \\(2^{O(B_{\\mathrm{sw}})}\\operatorname{poly}(N_{\\mathrm{in}}+B_{\\mathrm{sw}}+N_{\\mathcal O})\\), with one cached source-oracle reply per queried distinct protocol; in the infeasible case there is no certificate-output-length term.",
