    "justification": "The finite alternative distinguishes unattainability from high cost without a false polynomial-witness premise.",
    "gap": "A fixed-source decision does not decide existence over the priced physical catalogue.",
    "consumer": "A planner can certify that no legal acquired collection supports the target.",
    "proof_tex": "Let\n\\[\n \\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}\n =\\{E_{\\mathrm{sw}}:\\operatorname{Acc}_{\\mathrm{sw}}(Q,E_{\\mathrm{sw}};G)=1\\}.\n\\]\nIf \\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\neq\\varnothing\\), the feasible-case theorem returns \\(E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star}\\) and \\(\\operatorname{Opt}_{\\mathrm{sw}}=\\operatorname{Cost}(E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star})<+\\infty\\).  If \\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}=\\varnothing\\), the convention in Definition \\(\\mathrm{Switching\\ optimal\\ acquisition\\ cost}\\) gives \\(\\operatorname{Opt}_{\\mathrm{sw}}=\\inf\\varnothing=+\\infty\\).  The two cases are disjoint and exhaustive.\n\nThe canonical switching-certificate lemma gives\n\\[\n \\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\neq\\varnothing\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\exists E_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\in\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}\n \\text{ with }N_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\leq B_{\\mathrm{sw}}.                              \\tag{8}\n\\]\nThe switching normal-form theorem further gives\n\\[\n \\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\neq\\varnothing\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\exists E_0\\text{ finite and correctly typed such that }\n \\operatorname{CTFIDU}^{+}(G,Q,\\mathcal R(E_0))\\text{ accepts}.                 \\tag{9}\n\\]\nNegating (8) and (9) proves both asserted infeasibility equivalences.  The same bounded-string enumeration and cached-oracle analysis as in the feasible-case theorem has running time\n\\[\n 2^{O(B_{\\mathrm{sw}})}\\operatorname{poly}(N_{\\mathrm{in}}+B_{\\mathrm{sw}}+N_{\\mathcal O}).\n\\]\nWhen no string is accepted, the algorithm emits only the negative decision, so no output-certificate length is present.",
